{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_docfigures_docfigures_py", "label": "docfigures.py \u2014 do the repository's own documents state true numbers?", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "59 pinned figures, ~3 s, exit 1 on drift. It exists because CLAUDE.md claimed 559 held against 431 ABSENT when the measured figures were 702 and 4, and four more had drifted the same way."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_stale_row", "label": "A STALE row means the tree is right and the sentence is old", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "None of the drifts it found was a fault in the corpus, which is exactly why a count in prose needs a program behind it."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_standing_artefacts_row", "label": "The row that pins no number", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every docs/*.md, top-level *.tsv and tools/*.py must be named in CLAUDE.md. An index-based splice once deleted five pointers, 5,757 characters, and every pinned figure still held \u2014 they were all still true with no sentence left to be true about."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_deletion_lesson", "label": "Ask of any check: what would a deletion look like here?", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A guard that pins values answers whether a number is still right and cannot answer whether a document is still whole; those are different questions needing different instruments."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_instrument_totals_row", "label": "The instrument totals, and why their own selftests miss them", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pointers.py and arith.py fixtures each pin an individual site, so a change in a corpus-wide total passes both without a word. The finding predicate is the union of census class and finding verdict \u2014 neither half alone gives 42."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_two_parse_rows", "label": "Two parse rows, censusing .py by parsing and never importing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A first pass reported 34 files that do not parse and read it as recovery quality; 28 of the 34 are valid Python 3.11 refuses. Counting against one interpreter would have been wrong about the corpus and the tool."}, {"id": "docs_docfigures_do_not_update_pin_alone", "label": "Do not update the pin alone", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Correcting the pin without the prose converts a real finding into a silent one, which is the failure this instrument was written to catch."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_docfigures_two_parse_rows", "target": "claude_six_unparseable_fragments", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_docfigures_two_parse_rows", "target": "claude_python_312_requirement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/DOCFIGURES.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_docfigures_docfigures_py", "target": "docs_coverage_chats_flag", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRAC